{"url": "https://basgenbio.com/kr/sub/policy/privacy.php", "content_type": "text/html; charset=UTF-8", "language_hint": "kr", "text": "바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO KR EN Biobank Novel Biomarkers Target Discovery Drug Response Drug Repurposing Drug Combination Company 회사개요 연혁 개요 특허 및 인증 오시는 길 News 공지사항 보도자료 학술자료 홍보자료 Career 팀문화 채용 절차 및 공고 Policy 개인정보취급방침 (주)바스젠바이오(이하 '회사')은 고객님의 개인정보를 중요시하며, \"정보통신망 이용촉진 및 정보보호\"에 관한 법률을 준수하고 있습니다. 회사는 개인정보취급방침을 개정하는 경우 웹사이트 팝업 공지를 통하여 공지할 것입니다. 본 방침은 2023년부터 시행됩니다. 수집하는 개인정보 항목 회사는 온라인문의를 통해 이용자의 정보 수집 및 확용을 위해 아래와 같은 개인정보를 수집하고 있습니다. 수집항목 : 제목, 이메일, 내용, 첨부파일, 접속 로그 개인정보 수집방법 : 온라인문의 개인정보의 수집 및 이용목적 회사는 수집한 개인정보를 다음의 목적을 위해 활용합니다. 온라인문의 및 서비스 조치 등, 이용자의 정보 활용 목적을 위함 입니다. 개인정보의 보유 및 이용기간 회사는 원칙적으로 개인정보 수집 및 이용목적이 달성된 후에는 해당 정보를 지체 없이 파기합니다. 단, 다음의 정보에 대해서는 아래의 명시한 기간 동안 보존합니다. 가. 회사 내부 방침에 의한 정보보유 사유 - 부정이용기록 보존 이유 : 부정 이용 방지 보존 기간 : 1년 나. 관련법령에 의한 정보보유 사유 상법, 전자상거래 등에서의 소비자보호에 관한 법률 등 관계법령의 규정에 의하여 보존할 필요가 있는 경우 회사는 관계법령에서 정한 일정한 기간 동안 회원정보를 보관합니다. 이 경우 회사는 보관하는 정보를 그 보관의 목적으로만 이용하며 보존기간은 아래와 같습니다. - 계약 또는 청약철회 등에 관한 기록 보존 이유 : 전자상거래 등에서의 소비자보호에 관한 법률 보존 기간 : 5년 - 대금결제 및 재화 등의 공급에 관한 기록 보존 이유 : 전자상거래 등에서의 소비자보호에 관한 법률 보존 기간 : 5년 - 전자금융 거래에 관한 기록 보존 이유 : 전자금융거래법 보존 기간 : 5년 - 소비자의 불만 또는 분쟁처리에 관한 기록 보존 이유 : 전자상거래 등에서의 소비자보호에 관한 법률 보존 기간 : 3년 개인정보의 파기절차 및 방법 회사는 원칙적으로 개인정보 수집 및 이용목적이 달성된 후에는 해당 정보를 지체없이 파기합니다. 파기절차 및 방법은 다음과 같습니다. 파기절차 이용자의 온라인문의 등을 위해 입력하신 정보는 목적이 달성된 후 별도의 DB로 옮겨져(종이의 경우 별도의 서류함) 내부 방침 및 기타 관련 법령에 의한 정보보호 사유에 따라(보유 및 이용기간 참조) 일정 기간 저장된 후 파기되어집니다. 파기방법 - 전자적 파일형태로 저장된 개인정보는 기록을 재생할 수 없는 기술적 방법을 사용하여 삭제합니다. - 종이에 출력된 개인정보는 분쇄기로 분쇄하거나 소각을 통하여 파기합니다. 개인정보 제공 회사는 이용자의 개인정보를 원칙적으로 외부에 제공하지 않습니다. 개인정보 자동수집 장치의 설치, 운영 및 그 거부에 관한 사항 회사는 귀하의 정보를 수시로 저장하고 찾아내는 ‘쿠키(cookie)’ 등을 운용합니다. 쿠키란 회사의 웹사이트를 운영하는데 이용되는 서버가 귀하의 브라우저에 보내는 아주 작은 텍스트 파일로서 귀하의 컴퓨터 하드디스크에 저장됩니다. 회사는 다음과 같은 목적을 위해 쿠키를 사용합니다. 쿠키 등 사용 목적 이용자의 접속 빈도나 방문 시간 등을 분석, 이용자의 취향과 관심분야를 파악 및 자취 추적, 각종 이벤트 참여 정도 및 방문 회수 파악 등을 통한 타켓 마케팅 및 개인 맞춤 서비스 제공 귀하는 쿠키 설치에 대한 선택권을 가지고 있습니다. 따라서, 귀하는 웹브라우저에서 옵션을 설정함으로써 모든 쿠키를 허용하거나, 쿠키가 저장될 때마다 확인을 거치거나, 아니면 모든 쿠키의 저장을 거부할 수도 있습니다. 쿠키 설정 거부 방법 쿠키 설정을 거부하는 방법으로는 회원님이 사용하시는 웹 브라우저의 옵션을 선택함으로써 모든 쿠키를 허용하거나 쿠키를 저장할 때마다 확인을 거치거나, 모든 쿠키의 저장을 거부할 수 있습니다. 설정방법 예(인터넷 익스플로어의 경우): 웹 브라우저 상단의 도구 > 인터넷 옵션 > 개인정보 단, 귀하께서 쿠키 설치를 거부하였을 경우 서비스 제공에 어려움이 있을 수 있습니다. 개인정보에 관한 민원서비스 회사는 고객의 개인정보를 보호하고 개인정보와 관련한 불만을 처리하기 위하여 아래와 같이 관련 부서 및 개인정보관리책임자를 지정하고 있습니다. 개인정보관리책임자 담당자 : 개인정보취급방침 담당자 이메일 : company@basgenbio.com 귀하께서는 회사의 서비스를 이용하시며 발생하는 모든 개인정보보호 관련 민원을 개인정보관리책임자 혹은 담당부서로 신고하실 수 있습니다. 회사는 이용자들의 신고사항에 대해 신속하게 충분한 답변을 드릴 것입니다. 기타 개인정보침해에 대한 신고나 상담이 필요하신 경우에는 아래 기관에 문의하시기 바랍니다. 1) 개인분쟁조정위원회 (https://www.kopico.go.kr / 국번없이 1833-6972) 2) 개인정보 침해신고센터 (https://privacy.kisa.or.kr / 국번없이 118) 3) 대검찰청 사이버범죄수사단 (https://www.spo.go.kr / 국번없이 1301) 4) 경찰청 사이버범죄 신고시스템(ECRM) (https://ecrm.police.go.kr / 국번없이 182)​ Address. 서울특별시 마포구 마포대로 109, 19층 오(101동)-1901호 Tel. 02-6447-0200 Fax. 070-8740-8888 Mail. company@basgenbio.com ⓒ 2023. Basgenbio Inc. All rights reserved. PRIVACY POLICY LOCATION"}
{"url": "https://basgenbio.com/en/sub/biobank/biobank.php", "content_type": "text/html; charset=UTF-8", "language_hint": "en", "text": "바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO EN KR Biobank Novel Biomarkers Target Discovery Drug Response Drug Repurposing Drug Combination Company Overview History Patents & certificates Location News Notice Press release Academic materials Newsletter Career Our Company Recruit Biobank From the K-Biobank to global biobanks, we are leading the platformization of databases by combining bio big data with analytical technology. COCD Platform (Clinico-Omics Cohort Database Platform) The COCD Platform is Basgenbio's cohort database platform, including a total of 730,000 clinico-omics data, centered around K-Biobank and global biobanks such as UKB and ADNI. This platform contains information on various diseases, including cancer, chronic diseases, and autoimmune diseases. COCD Platform K-Biobank Blood Sample (156K+) Clinical Data Diagnosis, Treatment, Prescription Drug Information Lifestyle Data Smoking, Alcohol Consumption, Exercise Status Genomic Data DNA Micro-array Data Other Biobank UK Biobank (500K+) Korean The Cancer Genome Atlas (TCGA) (10K+) Genomic DataAlzheimer's Disease Neuroimaging Initiative (ADNI) (2K+) Data Sources (Scheduled for Acquisition) Multi-Omics Data Genomics Metabolomics Proteomics Transcriptomics Microbiome … 50K Blood Sample (Rare Disease) 1K Blood Sample (Aging Biobank Cohort) UK Biobank (United Kingdom Biobank) 500K+ Support Research on Serious and Life-Threatening Illnesses Primarily British With Some Other Ethnic Groups Korean confidential K-Biobank 156K+ Genomics, Clinical and life style information for serous and life-threatening Illnesses Korean TCGA (The Cancer Genome Atlas) 10K+ Advance Understanding of Cancer Through Genomic and Clinical Data Diverse Ethnic Backgrounds ADNI (The Alzheimer’s Disease Neuroimaging Initiative) 2K+ Accelerate the Development of Effective Treatments and Diagnostics for Alzheimer’s Disease and Related Dementias Primarily Non-Hispanic With Some Other Ethnic Groups Rare Disease Biobank *Scheduled for Acquisition Aging Biobank Cohort *Scheduled for Acquisition Etc *Scheduled for Acquisition K-Biobank Largest Private Biobank in South Korea K-Biobank stores blood samples from 156,000 subjects collected since 2005 from various medical institutions, including Yonsei Medical Center, major university hospitals, and health checkup centers. Its data scope is being expanded by linking clinical records and lifestyle information accumulated in government agencies such as the National Health Insurance Service, National Cancer Center, and Statistics Korea. Basgenbio conducts research and development activities based on K-Biobank, including drug efficacy simulation. genetic and environmental factor analysis related to disease occurrence, and scientific research results related to disease prevention, diagnosis, treatment, and prognosis. *Year of Acquisition: 2021 UK Biobank World's Largest Private Biobank UK Biobank consists of a large-scale cohort database with genetic and health data from 500,000 residents across the UK. Basgenbio analyzes data from global biobanks like this for research on disease prediction , drug response marker, and drug target validation. *Year of Acquisition: 2021 ADNI Alzheimer's Disease Neuroimaging Initiative (ADNI) ADNI is a multi-institutional, longitudinal, and prospective research database involving research teams from 63 regions in the United States and Canada. It tracks the progression of Alzheimer's disease using brain imaging, biochemical, and genetic biomarkers. It includes information on normal cognitive aging, mild cognitive impairment, and early Alzheimer's disease patients, allowing for multidimensional analysis. Basgenbio analyzes ADNI data for the discovery of drug response markers and targets related to Alzheimer's disease, as well as external validation. *Year of Acquisition: 2021 TCGA The Cancer Genome Atlas (TCGA) TCGA is a project started in 2005 aimed at the integrated accumulation of cancer genetic mutation data and biological information analysis. It is operated by the U.S. National Cancer Institute (NCI) and the National Human Genome Research Institute (NHGRI). Basgenbio analyzes TCGA data for the discovery of drug response markers and drug targets related to cancer, as well as external validation of internal results. *Year of Acquisition: 2022 For research purposes K-BIOBANK UKB TCGA ADNI Total Number of Data * 3 Trillion 20 Trillion 9 Million 616 Trillion Total Capacity of Training Data ** 725 GB 2.6 TB 3 TB 1 TB Total Number of Subjects 156K+ 500K+ 10K+ 2K+ Start Date of Subject Recruitment 2005 Year 2006 Year 2005 Year 2004 Year Types of Genomic Data Micro-array Micro-array / Whole Genome Sequencing / Whole Exome Sequencing Micro-array / RNA sequencing / Whole Genome Sequencing / Whole Exome Sequencing Micro-array / Whole Genome Sequencing Calculated as 'Total number of Participants' x 'Number of Variables,' and it is represented in Millions, Billions, or Trillions. HDD (Hard Disk Drive) capacity occupied by raw data Credit Project Manager Sol Lee Address. 101-1901, 109, Mapo-daero, Mapo-gu, Seoul, Republic of Korea Tel. +82 2-6447-0200 Fax. 070-8740-8888 Mail. company@basgenbio.com ⓒ 2023. Basgenbio Inc. All rights reserved. PRIVACY POLICY LOCATION"}
{"url": "https://basgenbio.com/en/sub/biomarkers/biomarkers.php", "content_type": "text/html; charset=UTF-8", "language_hint": "en", "text": "바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO EN KR Biobank Novel Biomarkers Target Discovery Drug Response Drug Repurposing Drug Combination Company Overview History Patents & certificates Location News Notice Press release Academic materials Newsletter Career Our Company Recruit Novel Biomarkers Discovery of Time-Labeled Biomarkers Biomarkers with time factors can be applied to various healthcare fields, ranging from disease prediction and diagnosis to prognosis. TLBM (Time-Labeled BioMarker) TLBM (Time-Labeled BioMarker) allows for disease prevention solutions through predictive biomarkers and the rapid discovery of diagnostic biomarkers by comparing data before and after disease onset. By determining disease risk based on changes over time and lifestyle habits, to provide solutions for disease prevention and healthcare management can be provided. The discovered TLBM can be used to quickly identify disease diagnostic biomarkers that can be applied in actual clinical settings. Predictive Biomarker Diagnostic Biomarker Framework The TLBM framework utilizes time-series data to predict disease risk over time and offers a healthcare management solution that can manage risk by age group. Genetic risk score Time-integrated risk score Device and method for generating disease onset information based on time-dependent associations using a polygenic risk score (Application No. 10-2021-0148683) and 9 others.* TLBM Gastric Cancer Biomarker Case (out-licensing completed) The gastric cancer TLBM identified by Basgenbio has a risk ratio of more than 17 times for the group with high-risk compared to the normal group; its powerful advantage is the ability to screen the disease in relatively young age groups. 17 times Calculating disease risk For the group with risk traits, the risk is over 17 times higher. From ≥40 y/o Identifying high-risk disease segments by age group Risk increases rapidly from the age of 40 for both normal and group with high-risk. BAS-GC-0001 40-49 y/o 50-59 y/o 60-69 y/o RISK(CT) (N=226) Incidence rate 25.31% 40.50% 66.36% 95% CI 0.19-0.31 0.34-0.47 0.48-0.78 NORMAL(CC) (N=32,491) Incidence rate 0.31% 1.66% 16.62% 95% CI 0.00-0.00 0.01-0.02 0.12-0.21 TLBM Discovery and Commercialization Process Discovery Validation Out-Licensing Commercialization Disease Prediction and Health Management Business Early Disease Diagnosis Business Disease Diagnosis Business Disease Prognosis Prediction Business TLBM Pipeline Category Disease Marker Selecting Disease Discovering Biomarker Prediction Genetic Risk Calculating Age-Specific Risk Changes Cross Validating Licensing Out Cancer Gastric Cancer BAS-GC-0001~10 Completion of L/O Breast Cancer BAS-BC-0001~12 Patent Application Process Colorectal Cancer BAS-CRC-0001~10 Patent Application Process Liver Cancer BAS-LC-0001~10 Patent Application Process Thyroid Cancer BAS-TC-0001~10 Patent Application Process Prostate Cancer BAS-PC-0001~05 Patent Application Process Cardio- cerebrovasc ular Disease Ischemic Heart Disease BAS-IHD-0001~32 Patent Application Process Stroke BAS-STR-0001~08 Patent Application Process Acute Myocardial Infarcation BAS-aMI-0001~12 Patent Application Process Autoimmune Disease Inflammatory Bowel Disease BAS-IBD-XXXX Rheumatold Arthritis BAS-RA-XXXX Metabolic Disease Gout BAS-GT-XXXX Credit Project Manager Jungoh Kim, Ph.D. Project Assistant Jihye Lee Data Analyst Eunbyeol Lee, Yujeong Shim Address. 101-1901, 109, Mapo-daero, Mapo-gu, Seoul, Republic of Korea Tel. +82 2-6447-0200 Fax. 070-8740-8888 Mail. company@basgenbio.com ⓒ 2023. Basgenbio Inc. All rights reserved. PRIVACY POLICY LOCATION"}
{"url": "https://basgenbio.com/en/sub/discovery/discovery.php", "content_type": "text/html; charset=UTF-8", "language_hint": "en", "text": "바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO EN KR Biobank Novel Biomarkers Target Discovery Drug Response Drug Repurposing Drug Combination Company Overview History Patents & certificates Location News Notice Press release Academic materials Newsletter Career Our Company Recruit Target Discovery Target Discovery for Diseases and Drugs We identify target proteins most closely associated with disease occurrence and conduct optimized analyses for rapid drug development. Framework Understanding the causes of diseases within biological systems and evaluating candidate genes that can serve as drug targets. Discovering high-potential drug targets using three core technologies: Multi-omics analysis, causal inference, and AI algorithms. Basgenbio boasts an optimized target discovery system for drug development by combining Basgenbio cohort/real-world data, and AI technology. DEEPCT™ Credit Project Manager Jungoh Kim, Ph.D. Project Assistant Jihye Lee Project Leader Sunyeop Lee Data Analyst Eunbyeol Lee, Yujeong Shim Address. 101-1901, 109, Mapo-daero, Mapo-gu, Seoul, Republic of Korea Tel. +82 2-6447-0200 Fax. 070-8740-8888 Mail. company@basgenbio.com ⓒ 2023. Basgenbio Inc. All rights reserved. PRIVACY POLICY LOCATION"}
{"url": "https://basgenbio.com/en/sub/response/response.php", "content_type": "text/html; charset=UTF-8", "language_hint": "en", "text": "바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO EN KR Biobank Novel Biomarkers Target Discovery Drug Response Drug Repurposing Drug Combination Company Overview History Patents & certificates Location News Notice Press release Academic materials Newsletter Career Our Company Recruit Drug Response Marker Discovery for Drug Responders/Non-Responders Basgenbio predicts drug responders and non-responders by developing algorithms for drug effectiveness, applicable to personalized medicine development. Framework Identifying biomarkers that classify drug responders and non-responders is an essential technology for developing personalized treatments. Case of Drug Response Biomarker Discovery (Antidepressants) * RCT : Randomized Clinical Trial Response Marker Interaction GWAS Comparative Analysis of Antidepressant Responders vs. Non-Responders Exploration of Antidepressant Resistance-Related Markers Resistant, Non-Resistant Interaction Filtering Final set of 27 markers established. Classifier Performance Comparison and Performance Analysis of Resistance Group Marker Gene Scores Resistant Group Prediction Performance AUC: 0.63 Credit Project Manager Jungoh Kim, Ph.D. Project Assistant Hyunjoon Lim Project Leader Sanghyuck Yoon Data Analyst Jiwon Lim, Jihi Cha Address. 101-1901, 109, Mapo-daero, Mapo-gu, Seoul, Republic of Korea Tel. +82 2-6447-0200 Fax. 070-8740-8888 Mail. company@basgenbio.com ⓒ 2023. Basgenbio Inc. All rights reserved. PRIVACY POLICY LOCATION"}
{"url": "https://basgenbio.com/en/sub/combination/combination.php", "content_type": "text/html; charset=UTF-8", "language_hint": "en", "text": "바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO EN KR Biobank Novel Biomarkers Target Discovery Drug Response Drug Repurposing Drug Combination Company Overview History Patents & certificates Location News Notice Press release Academic materials Newsletter Career Our Company Recruit Drug Combination Optimization of Drug Combination Basgenbio presents new combination of drugs with maximum efficacy at the same time as minimum adverse drug reactions through drug-drug interaction analyses. Framework Leveraging years’ worth of Prescription Data, Mendelian Randomization, Network Analysis, and AI Algorithm, optimum drug combinations are suggested. It recommends the best drug combinations by integrating drug efficacy, possible adverse drug reactions, and marketability. COMBI FINDER Simultaneous considerations in marketability and combined drug effects are implemented through analysis of prescription data (from 2 to N drug combination therapies). Recommendations based on target diseases and active drug ingredients. CANDIDATE A INGRED 1 INGRED 2 INGRED 3 CANDIDATE B INGRED 4 INGRED 5 INGRED 6 CANDIDATE C INGRED 7 INGRED 8 INGRED 9 Recommendation of optimized combination structures of drug compounds. Confirmation of existing combination drugs (fixed-dose combinations of 2 to N drugs). DEEPCT Comparison of clinical outcome between no treatment, monotherapy, or combination therapy groups Example of Visualized Results Credit Project Manager Jungeun Kim AI algorithm Developer Jiyeon Kim, Suhan Cho Project Leader Suhan Cho Network analysis Jiyeon Kim, Yujeong Shim Address. 101-1901, 109, Mapo-daero, Mapo-gu, Seoul, Republic of Korea Tel. +82 2-6447-0200 Fax. 070-8740-8888 Mail. company@basgenbio.com ⓒ 2023. Basgenbio Inc. All rights reserved. PRIVACY POLICY LOCATION"}
{"url": "https://basgenbio.com/en/sub/company/overview.php", "content_type": "text/html; charset=UTF-8", "language_hint": "en", "text": "바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO EN KR Biobank Novel Biomarkers Target Discovery Drug Response Drug Repurposing Drug Combination Company Overview History Patents & certificates Location News Notice Press release Academic materials Newsletter Career Our Company Recruit Company Basgenbio proposes value beyond health through Biological Big data. Basgenbio leads innovative disease prevention method and drug development using AI technology implemented with vast amount of data from Global Biobank as well as K-Biobank. Key Personnel Management Team Il-Tae Jang CEO Chief executive officer Medical Doctor Chairman of Nanoori Medical Foundation Understanding the root causes of diseases through immense medical data and genetic information stored in blood. Basgenbio aims to take a leading role in the fields of preventive and precision medicine by leveraging AI and Biological Big data. The goal is to pioneer in new healthcare market by combining genomic and medical data, thus extending the lifespan and improving quality of life of humanity. To achieve this, Basgenbio continuously develops and enhances the AI algorithms and conducts Big data analysis to find the causes and treatments of various diseases. We are dedicated to enhancing healthcare and pursuit happiness through the fusion of AI technology and biomedicine. Ho Kim CEO Genetic epidemiology R&D Extending healthy human life based on clinical genomic cohort data. By developing appropriate therapeutic drugs through biomarker discovery, Basgenbio focuses on predicting the occurrence and progression of diseases over time. We explore the potential of future medicine based on genomic cohort data and proprietary technology, aiming to lead an active and creative medical approaches in response to diseases. Haeng Seok Yoo Vice President Chief Financial Officer Establishing transparent financial management and accurate investment strategies. Basgenbio has secured genetic cohort data that is not easily obtainable by anyone in the era of data competition. Although there are still many problems to be solved to use this valuable data efficiently, Basgenbio is highly commended for their direction and growth. We promise to make active efforts to extend the 'healthy lifespan' of human. Jung-Eun Kim Head of AI Drug Development Division Head of division, AI Drug Development Division Broadening the possibilities of future medicine by analyzing genomic and epidemiological data. Basgenbio strives to derive meaningful results using human genomic and epidemiological data as in silico analysis specialists. We value communication and collaboration with our clients and flexibly adapt to various situations. As one of the leaders in drug development, drug efficacy simulation, and biomarker discovery, we expand the possibilities of future medicine with top-tier data and technology. Advisory Board Eun-Hee Ha M.D., Ph.D. Outside Director / Medical / Environmental Advisory Board Based on genomic cohort data, extending healthy human life. Professor Eun-hee Ha, after obtaining her doctorate in Preventive Medicine and 28 years of tenure at Ewha Womans University, conducted continuous Basic and Policy Research based on her academic interests in Environmental Epidemiology and Medicine, and Environmental Health Policy. In particular, in 2015, she consolidated her research capabilities and received recognition as a leading expert in the field of Environmental Medicine, establishing the National Children’s Environmental Health Birth Cohort Support Center and laying the foundation for the Korean nationwide birth cohort. She has published over 160 papers in international SCI journals, received the Presidential Commendation for Environmental Conservation in 2009, the National Medal in 2018 from the Korea Ministry of Environment. She also received the Ewha Academic Award in 2019 and is currently serving as the 26th Dean of the College of Medicine at Ewha Womans University. Won-il Jeong Ph.D. Statistics Advisory Board Professor Won-il Jeong obtained a master's degree in Natural Science at Seoul National University followed by a Ph.D. in Medical Statistics at University of North Carolina in the United States. He later worked as a Research Fellow at Harvard University. Subsequently, he served as an Assistant Professor at the Department of Information Statistics and Actuarial Science at Soongsil University, leading various research projects in medical and genetic statistics. He is also actively involved at the Korean Statistical Society (KSS) and the Korea Genome Organization (KOGO). To this day, he has led numerous research projects and played a leading role in genomics-based statistical research. Address. 101-1901, 109, Mapo-daero, Mapo-gu, Seoul, Republic of Korea Tel. +82 2-6447-0200 Fax. 070-8740-8888 Mail. company@basgenbio.com ⓒ 2023. Basgenbio Inc. All rights reserved. PRIVACY POLICY LOCATION"}
{"url": "https://basgenbio.com/en/sub/company/history.php", "content_type": "text/html; charset=UTF-8", "language_hint": "en", "text": "바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오는 K-Biobank를 기반으로 다양한 글로벌 바이오뱅크 데이터를 지속적으로 추가하여 자체 솔루션과 기술을 개발하고 검증합니다\n바스젠바이오 BASGENBIO EN KR Biobank Novel Biomarkers Target Discovery Drug Response Drug Repurposing Drug Combination Company Overview History Patents & certificates Location News Notice Press release Academic materials Newsletter Career Our Company Recruit Company History 2023 2022 2021 2020 2019 2018 2023 Nominated as the 'SUPERSTART Incubator' by the 2nd LG Open-Innovation Start-up Nurture Program Global Joint License & Technical Assistance and Asset Validation of Aging-related Sarcopenia Treatment Candidate with KSB Tugen Nominated as '2023 Korea AI Startup 100' in Healthcare Sector by The Korea Economic Daily X KT MOU for AI-based Bio-Bigdata Commercialization with Hancomcarelink & 3BIGS [Celltrion] joint R&D and SI agreements for genomics-based biomarker discovery. Nominated as ‘Core 100’ by Seoul Investment Promotion Agency. Nominated as a COREBIZ company by Korea SMEs Development Association. Nominated for the 2nd IKMP (Invest Korea Marketplace) project in 2023, organized by KOTRA (Korea Trade-Investment Promotion Agency). Chosen as the Global Innovation Center in Silicon Valley's PMF program, under the Korea Ministry of Science and ICT (MSIT) Nominated as ‘Baby Unicorn 200’ by the Ministry of SMEs and Startups (MSS) 2022 [National Project] Participated in the AI-Integrated Medical Imaging Diagnosis System Project. - Participating company for the AI Voucher Support Project 2022. - Participating company for the AI-Integrated Medical Imaging Diagnosis System Project (Femoral Fracture). [Genomics Company] Licensing agreement for gastric cancer biomarkers. - Winner, 2nd Place, of the Amgen Korea X Ministry of Health and Welfare 'Pitching Day’. [Allico Pharmaceutical] MOU for joint development of AI-based new drug based on genomic cohort data. - Winner, 1st Place, Novartis X Seoul City '3rd Health X Challenge Seoul’. [Samjin Pharmaceutical] Joint research MOU for AI-based new drug development. 2021 [National Project] Participated in the AI-Integrated Medical Imaging Diagnosis System project. - Exclusive contract for the use of Genomic Cohort Data. - Licensing agreement with Yonsei Medical Center. - Changed the company name to BASGENBIO. [DS Asset Management] Raised a Series A Funding Round. [Ewha Medical Center] MOU for research on the Genomic Cohort and EMR data. [Korea University Medical Center] MOU for research and development of an AI-based Precision Medical Convergence Platform. 2020 [National Project] Participated in the AI-Integrated Medical Imaging Diagnosis System Project. - Developed AI-based Genomic Data Analysis Tool at Yonsei University Graduate School of Public Health. 2019 Joint R&D for genomic data at Yonsei Medical Center. 2018 Established 2BKO, a joint-stock company. Development of a Rare Disease Platform Project at Korea University. Address. 101-1901, 109, Mapo-daero, Mapo-gu, Seoul, Republic of Korea Tel. +82 2-6447-0200 Fax. 070-8740-8888 Mail. company@basgenbio.com ⓒ 2023. Basgenbio Inc. All rights reserved. PRIVACY POLICY LOCATION"}
